{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553030-does-a-digital-footprint-hurt-you-in-employment","id":1553030,"title":"Does a digital footprint hurt you in employment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-09T12:19:20-07:00","id":1553030,"title":"Does a digital footprint hurt you in employment?","content":"I'm showing my age here, but when I entered the workforce it was showing your work history and a list of references and not to mention selling yourself in a job interview if one was lucky enough.<br /> <br /> Now I heard about that the type of digital footprint can hurt your chances for employment or even getting further schooling. Do companies ask about your social media history at all?<br /> <br /> My last interview at the current job I'm at, it never came up at all and that might be due to my age as I entered the workforce way before this was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T13:05:41-07:00","id":1553034,"title":"","content":"That depends. Depends on the job, the company, the country, and the nature of this footprint.<br /> <br /> And they won't ask you. Any company that asks about your digital history is just showing their incompetence.<br /> <br /> What they do is to seek it out themselves, and that's usually quite easy to do. When they chose to be open about that (which isn't always the case), they'll have your social media history with them already at the interview. You may be asked about things you posted or liked, etc.. You may be required to contextualize or discuss some, you may be just oriented on what to change and what to keep doing, or you may be told a given internet behavior was a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> Sometimes they won't bring it at all, or minimize the impact in the interview, but that doesn't mean they're evaluating you partially (or a lot) based on what you do on the internet.<br /> <br /> Finally, and unfortunately, this can cut in any direction. The same behavior that's a no deal for some companies may be actively wanted by others. Some want to distance themselves from political militancy, for example, while others seek to fill the payroll with political allies, and that's for any political stance at all: you may make it or break it because you're progressive, conservative, pacifist, militaristic, socialist or full on nazi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-09T15:10:17-07:00","id":1553035,"title":"","content":"Social media definitely is getting more impactful for employment than it used to be, but companies ultimately don't want to deal with backlash because they hired someone that has some bad takes, etc.<br /> <br /> Though I've certainly had a history where it hit me and my coworkers way sooner than it's starting to hit the broad population. But that's because what I used to do involved children (even if I rarely interacted with children directly, and never without supervision of other adults). The scrutiny they put people that deal with children under is always a good sign of what everyone else is going to be looking at having to deal with in ~10 years. Once it's normal to scour one group's social media as part of employment, it's easier to consider doing it to other related groups (teachers had it worse than we did). Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T08:38:24-07:00","id":1553218,"title":"","content":"A law-firm I applied for wanted my passwords to my social media account so they can verify. I laughed if they're going to treat me like that, what else are they going to expect if I work for them. So, I put a huge LGBT (Rainbow-flag), as my main picture so if they actually did looked up my social-media, they'd be essentially asking an illegal-question and I could successfully ligate against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T14:20:45-07:00","id":1553223,"title":"","content":"I think here in Brazil just asking your passwords for social media is already illegal.<br /> <br /> Not saying it doesn't happen. A lot of ridiculously illegal abuse happen in the job market, for several reasons, but it would be a fast path to litigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T06:05:51-07:00","id":1553398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553030-does-a-digital-footprint-hurt-you-in-employment#post1553030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I heard about that the type of digital footprint can hurt your chances for employment or even getting further schooling. Do companies ask about your social media history at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been in my current job for like 16 years now, but I have interviewed for a few new jobs in the last few years. Luckily social media never came up, or at least they never asked me about it... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1553030-does-a-digital-footprint-hurt-you-in-employment?p=1553218#post1553218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A law-firm I applied for wanted my passwords to my social media account so they can verify. I laughed if they're going to treat me like that, what else are they going to expect if I work for them. So, I put a huge LGBT (Rainbow-flag), as my main picture so if they actually did looked up my social-media, they'd be essentially asking an illegal-question and I could successfully ligate against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, that's crazy! What the hell? I'm not giving any place or anyone the logins to any any of my accounts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"